a little like  thing i pull out and then i put a  squeezy tube down into my mouth and then  i can drink from a bottle just how  uncomfortable can wearing a spider-man  suit be every spider-man film has  boasted an extremely vibrant collection  of characters equipped with some  state-of-the-art costumes and makeup  from those tight spidey suits to those  gruesome villainous prosthetics the  stars of the spider-man movies had to  get quite uncomfortable when portraying  their on-screen personas i was just like  swinging about in this super creepy way  and like trying to  trying to talk to peter who wouldn't  want to suit up as spider-man it was our  childhood dream to put on the iconic red  and blue suit and that was no different  for star tom holland i feel like my  whole life had been leading up to me  trying on this suit despite the  excitement wearing the suit on set did  come with some setbacks in fact holland  believes that he has the hardest suit to  wear out of anyone in the marvel  universe whenever holland has the  classic suit on he's covered head to toe  in lycra with no skin showing i can't  even use my phone  and i'm 23 like i use my phone a lot in  fact polland isn't even able to scratch  an itch on his face in the costume it's  just one of the costs of being  spider-man it looks amazing it feels  terrible the costume designers behind  the mysterio suit wanted to make sure  that it was as practical as possible  since the bulky costume wasn't  particularly the most comfortable fit  the producers assumed that gyllenhaal  wouldn't want to be wearing the  villain's threads in too many scenes you  know it's like wearing a ball gown  grab your ba you're all of a sudden  choked by this right though gyllenhaal  was more than willing and even a little  excited to bear through the discomfort  and wear the mysterio costume whenever  he would see fit so not only is this  costume practical but he wears it  everywhere it makes sense to wear it so  we think this looks amazing  it took a little bit of time to put on  but once it was on yeah it made me feel  pretty strong it wasn't just alfred  molina who took on the persona of doc  ock director sam raimi wanted the  villain's trademark claws to actually be  practical effects which led to  puppeteers acting around molina to make  his robotic tentacles look more alive  molina needed to do rehearsals in  costumes so he could get accustomed to  moving around in the complicated suit  people understand how much the actors  are doing because you think oh it's all  magical cgi stuff topher grace had to  undergo a grueling makeup process to  become the iconic spider-man villain  venom for the third film in the original  trilogy i had four hours of prosthetic  makeup every morning when i was venom  and just getting on the suit takes about  45 minutes before that so i had to get  there at three or something grace also  had to go through an extensive workout  routine to gain around 20 pounds for the  roll  in order for dane dehaan to become the  grotesque and slimy green goblin the  makeup took over three hours initial  designs for the gross looking villain  had dehaan taking on an even greener  look as the iconic spider-man villain  but the makeup department decided to go  for a look that felt more slightly human  than full-on goblin that's how i started  out like you know playing pretend and  dressing up as superheroes dane dehaan's  goblin suit weighed 50 pounds and took  an hour to put on the set where de haan  was required to be in his goblin get-up  was over a hundred degrees fahrenheit  and because of the extreme conditions  dehan lost seven pounds in just two days  now that's impressive  jamie foxx had the distinct advantage of  having two distinctive styles as max  dillon aka electro in the amazing  spider-man 2 but it was his villain's  nerdy alter ego that was internally  painful for typically sleek and smooth  fox fox dubbed his hair on set as the  first black comb over and he also  sported a gap in his teeth when i was  max on the streets girls are like look  at jamie foxx at that hair oh my god  something is off with him at the same  time fox was at least somewhat relieved  that he wouldn't be as bombarded with  attention since he figured there'd be  plenty of people who wouldn't recognize  him honestly though most people would be  able to recognize jamie foxx no matter  the makeup hey y'all tell everybody  electro's in town the makeup department  behind jamie foxx's electro look had to  get very experimental in order to  prevent inhibiting fox's performance as  the blue skinned villain very thin  pieces of silicone were applied all over  fox's body in order for the look to be  much more believable on top of the  silicone fox had to wear glowing blue  contact lenses it was a great choice to  be in this film and i'm i'm happy and  fortunate that they that they chose me  while rhys  full lizard form was mostly cgi there  still was plenty of makeup work to be  done for the transitioning stages of the  villain ifans would spend up to seven to  eight hours in the makeup chair to  complete his green scaly look after  seven hours in a chair with not enough  cigarettes i was kind of in the right  mental state to play a man who was about  to transform into a nine foot lizard  with a dangerous tail the prosthetics  caused a lot of chafing on ifan's body  which led him to walking around like a  cowboy for several days after filming  after all there has to be some side  effects from becoming the lizard  marvel was extremely strict about what  holland was supposed to wear underneath  his costume during holland's first day  on set he was given thongs by the crew  as the only thing he could wear under  the spiderman costume i had serious  misgivings would my art ever be the same  again but i had to get used to it  secondly i have to wear  essentially pajamas michael keaton's  vulture suit stands out in how it  combines the classic marvel style with  something a bit more grounded i can't  tell you there are hundreds maybe of  little screws literally that special  wrenches made to put the boots in a  certain way a costume this intricate  took quite some time to fully equip on  heaton i don't know what my favorite  costume was because it's like what 7 30.  i'm barely awake i barely know where i  am andrew garfield wasn't necessarily  thrilled the first time he put on his  spider-man suit the suit he wore was  made of a material that was designed to  make you irritated on top of that  garfield suit was skin tight which led  to more of his body being visible to the  public than we would have preferred one  of the first nights we were out on  location in downtown l.a we were in a  parking structure i knew there were  paparazzi taking terrible unflattering  shots of my you know everything it was  an acting exercise  it was just a lot to uh to hold i i  struggled to hold it all i kind of  rejected it a lot rules were so strict  that holland claimed that even simply  drinking water in the spidey suit was  dangerous this led to holland and the  costume designers having to brainstorm  ways to adapt as obviously holland would  need some fluids while filming in the  heat  i can kind of get it i've had a kit kat  in the suit now the left eye on the  spidey costume would have a squeezy tube  attached that holland would have to pull  out and put into his mouth so he could  get a drink of water how refreshing  i loved in spider-man particularly  playing the double roll willem dafoe is  known for his very distinguishable  jawline so when playing norman osborne  in the first sam raimi spider-man movie  he needed to look more like how the  billionaire character looked in the  comics defoe was given dental  prosthetics to make his teeth look  straighter as the main villain though  the prosthetics were removed whenever  his character would look at himself in  the mirror and they were really fun to  do while willem dafoe surprisingly did  not need much prosthetic work done the  acclaimed thespian still had some  discomfort about the green goblin's  technologically advanced costume defoe  called his experience in costume severe  though he still had a great time on set  whenever tom holland put on that  spider-man suit he knew there was no  going back for him in many ways like  having to wait to go to the bathroom an  accident is not an option that suit is  so expensive they'll be so upset with me  in fact holland would have to plan going  to take a bathroom break 45 minutes in  advance hopefully there were no  accidents while filming toby maguire  wore the iconic red and blue spider-man  suit over the course of three films just  because he had a longer tenure as the  character than somebody like andrew  garfield that didn't make the suit any  more comfortable in fact the black  symbiote suit that maguire wore in the  third film proved to be the most  uncomfortable suit of them all it can  ride up in the crotch a little bit it's  not really the outerwear of the suit  it's the inner bit that rides up well at  least it wasn't flash thompson giving  the wedgies this time  toby maguire holds the title of being  the first actor to portray spider-man on  the big screen and with that the costume  designers were still trying to work  through crafting the perfect spider-man  costume in order to get the costume  right the designers had to do a full  body cast of maguire which wasn't the  most fun experience for the actor i had  to stand there for a couple of hours and  then the stuff sticking to the hair on  my body and they ripped it off and it  was extremely painful maguire even  initially had a hard time acting with  the spider-man mask on though he was  able to get used to it quite quickly  while andrew garfield's comics accurate  spider-man suit may have been a fan  favorite in the amazing spider-man 2 it  was far from comfortable for garfield to  wear it was a very specific experience  and  i imagine um  it'll be different every time garfield  blamed his british reverse on the reason  why he was uncomfortable in the costume  spandex does not suit the british you  are pretty much naked so you have to  trust what you have is enough  paul giamatti's rhino suit required  plenty of cgi but that didn't prevent  his onset appearance from being an  uncomfortable one in fact giamatti's  costume while filming required him to be  attached to a large metal-like structure  some of which he'd wear with backpack  straps  there's clearly a lot that goes into  making these spider-man characters look  as good as they do from hours-long  makeup applications to extravagant  prosthetics and uncomfortable costumes  the franchise's biggest stars were able  to power through their discomfort when  bringing the famous web head to life

